  "review_changes": [
    "F1: src/cli.bend refuses encoded calldata over 131072 bytes with exit 64 and \"calldata exceeds 131072 bytes\" before encoding. The test adds a 130977-byte string refusal, a 4096-word refusal and a 131044-byte accepted string checked against cast.",
    "F2: dev/M2-CALLDATA-CLI.md says arguments must be valid UTF-8 and the Node.js host replaces invalid sequences with U+FFFD. The runtime is unchanged.",
    "F3: dev/calldata-cli-test.py requires \"truncated value\" for every truncated tuple row with a complete selector.",
    "F4: dev/calldata-cli-test.py checks that a 131072-byte decoding input passes the cap and fails on trailing data, and refuses an unprefixed 131073-byte input.",
    "F5: the record keeps verbatim copies of check-static.py, check-cli-regressions.py and prepare-validation.py, and README.md says what they ran.",
    "F6: README.md and dev/ASSAY-M2-BUILD-LOG.md say that the initial make test ran on the src/call_cli.bend layout and which components ran alone.",
    "F7: dev/M2-CALLDATA-CLI.md gives the limit of 78 decimal or 64 hexadecimal digits, including leading zeroes.",
    "marker: CALLDATA-CLI encode=53 decode=55 oracle=cast refusals=196 pin_mutants=2 OK",
    "logs: review-build.log, review-compiled-assay.json, review-calldata-cli.log, review-event-decode-cli.log, review-event-cli.log, review-mapping-cli.log, review-milestone-speed.log, review-gates.log"
  ]
